# 2026-08-27: added after a past session's local tooling silently rewrote
# ~60 unrelated files with CRLF line endings and a spurious +x bit, none of
# which had any real content change — it took a full manual file-by-file
# review to separate that noise from the handful of genuine fixes mixed in
# with it. Normalizing line endings in git itself (not just relying on an
# editor setting) stops this recurring silently the same way again.
* text=auto eol=lf
